# What Vercel uploads is what it uploads. Keep it to what the build needs.
#
# The first deploy attempt aborted partway through a 2.9 MB upload, and Vercel
# was auto-detecting this repository as **Python** — because `contracts/`,
# `scripts/`, `conftest.py` and `pyproject.toml` all sit at the root. None of
# them are involved in building the interface.
#
# So: the deployment contains the frontend and the contract, and nothing else.
# The contract is kept because it is the thing the frontend reads, and a
# reviewer arriving from the deployment URL can see it. Everything else is
# reachable from the repository.

# The contract source and its docs — the subject of the product.
!contracts/
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/VERIFICATION.md
!README.md
!vercel.json

# Everything below is development machinery that a build never reads.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
tests/
state/
frontend/.m5-verify-build/
frontend/dist/
scripts/
conftest.py
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt
requirements-dev.txt
gltest.config.yaml
run_direct_tests.sh
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.keystore